$DATUM SYNTHESIS OF DIBENZO-14-CROWN-4.6 1,2-dihydroxybenzene (1.21 g, 0.011
mol), sodium hydroxide (0.8 g, 0.02 mol), and 1,3-dichloropropane (1.12,
0.01 mol) were mixed in DMSO (1 mL). The mixture was placed in a
household microwave oven for 8 min. The crude product was taken up in
conc. HCl (2 mL) and filtered. The filtrate was extracted with CHCl3,
dried, and evaporated to afford a crude residue, which was crystallized
from n-heptane to afford the title compound. Yield 72%.
DIBENZO-14-CROWN-4.6. Yield 72%. m.p. 150, 150-152 lit.1a IR (KBr disc)
3000, 1600, 1450, 1420, 1300, 900 cm-1. 1HNMR, δ (CDCl3) 2.25 (s, 4H,
CH2), 4.25 (t, 8H, CH2), M, m/z, M+, 300.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile and rapid synthesis of some crown ethers under microwave
irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
