$DATUM [(3S,4S)-3-Benzyloxy-4-ethynyloxy-7,7-dimethoxy-heptyloxy]-tert-butyl-dimethyl-silane
(6) A suspension of mineral oil-free potassium hydride (347 mg, 8.65
mmol) in THF (10 mL) was cooled to 0 °C and treated with a solution of
the secondary alcohol (1.55 g, 3.76 mmol) in THF (10 mL). After 1 h at 0
°C the mixture was cooled to –78 °C and trichloroethylene (395 μL, 4.14
mmol) was added dropwise. The solution was allowed to warm up to rt
whereupon it turned dark brown. It was stirred for 1 h at rt, then again
cooled to –78 °C and methyllithium (1.66 M in Et2O, 5.7 mL, 9.40 mmol)
was added. After stirring at this temperature for 30 min it was allowed
to warm up to –40 °C over a 30 min period and was stirred again for 30
min. The reaction was quenched by adding MeOH (1.5 mL, 38 mmol) and
warmed to rt. The mixture was diluted with TBME (50 mL) and subjected to
aqueous workup using sat. NaHCO3-solution (30 mL) and TBME (3 × 40 mL).
Drying of the combined organic layers with Na2SO4 and subsequent flash
chromatography on basic alumina (pentane/Et2O 6:1) afforded the ynolether
6 (1.176 g, 2.71 mmol, 72%) as a colorless oil that was used immediately
for the next transformation. R f= 0.35 (pentane/TBME 5:1). [α]D = –20.0
(c = 1.40, CHCl3, ϑ = 20°C). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.36-7.25 (m,
5H), 4.67 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J = 11.2 Hz, 1H), 4.37 (t, J =
5.0 Hz, 1H), 4.15-4.08 (m, 1H), 3.90 (ddd, J = 8.7, 5.0, 4.0 Hz, 1H),
3.73 (dd, J = 7.1, 5.1 Hz, 2H), 3.32 (s, 3H), 3.31 (s, 3H), 1.87-1.61 (m,
6H), 1.55 (s, 1H), 0.90 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 6H). 13CNMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 138.3, 128.3 (2C), 128.0 (2C), 127.7, 104.1, 92.0, 90.5, 75.7, 73.3,
59.0, 53.0, 52.6, 33.1, 28.3, 27.1, 25.9 (3C), 24.5, 18.2, –5.36, –5.41.
HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C24H40NaO5Si (M+Na+): 436.2645, found:
436.2643.
