$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General method for the synthesis of
2-aryloxy-N,N-diethyletanamine hydrochlorides. A mixture of 0.1 mole of
the corresponding phenol. 70 ml toluene, 0.1 mole of hydrochloride or
hydrobromide (2-chloro- or 2-bromo-, respectively) of
N,N-diethylethanamine, and 12.5 g of comminuted NaOH was boiled with
stirring for 8 h on a sand bath, cooled, alkalized with a NaOH solution
until obtaining an alkaline reaction, and extracted with ether (150 ml).
The ether - toluene extract was washed with NaOH solution until complete
discoloration of the aqueous phase. The organic layer was dried over
crystalline NaOH and filtered. The filtrate was purged with dry HCl and
the precipitated 2-aryloxy-N,N-diethyletanamine hydrochloride was
separated by filtration, washed with ether, and crystallized from an
appropriate solvent. In cases where no solvent for crystallization can be
found, the product is purified by converting it onto the base form and
repeated purging with dry HCl. Compound XXVIII, yield 71.4%. Empirical
formula: C12H18FNO.HCl; M.p. 139 - 140°C (toluene); 1H NMR δ, ppm
(CDCl3): 1.377 t (6H, N(CH2CH3)2), 3.112 - 3.390 m (6H, CH2N(CH2CH3)2),
4.392 t (2H, OCH2CH2), 6.520 - 7.466 m (4H, arom. H), 12.15 bs (1H, NH+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antimicrobial activity of 2-aryloxy-N,N-diethylethanamine
derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Semenovykh, E. V.; Pantsurkin, V. I.; Novikova, V. V.; Odegova, T. F.;
Syropyatov, B. Ya.; Vakhrin, M. I.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Pharmaceutical Chemistry Journal (2007), 41(4), 211-215

